<p>Honestly I want to second this. Those three paragraphs need to be rewritten.</p>
<p>Some of my issues I've had reading this article that made me not upvote are:</p>
<ul>
<li>If they're indistinguishable except for their effects, and we really don't know what two and three really do (arguably, three's the only one that we definitely don't know what it does) how do we even know there's three different types, and not different reactions to the same type? It might be better explained as 'there's a small chance of this happening in every ██.█% of test subjects,' but that's just one suggestion of how you could handle that.</li>
<li>The numbering should really start at SCP-3287-1 for the instruction manual and 2-4 for the compounds made, because the instructions are part of the SCP, but that's nitpicky.</li>
<li>The unicorn horn is way to similar to this SCP without making changes as to how this SCP works. You do have the advantage that the unicorn horn is a natural resource rather than a synthetic once, but it would be easiest to make a distinction between the effects of the unicorn horn and the effects of the gas when you go to edit the paragraphs for the first bullet.</li>
